In the business world, smart homes have made a fierce entry in the real estate market. Particularly in areas such as Abu Dhabi, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Singapore and Hong Kong. These are the biggest profile countries when it comes to the implementation of futuristic lifestyles in accordance to large scale smart- home developments. Phase 1 of developments generally began amidst the 2000s to the early 2010s; this was a time when automation was a luxury custom installed niche. Few had access and almost all systems were individually tailored to high profile clients. Phase 2 commenced from 2012-2019; this marked a new chapter where cheap installments such as LED bulb, home surveillance and voice assistance were introduced into more average households. 
A large debate occurs in the business world rooting from the discussion whether incooperating smart products and systems in homes qualify as a "smart house" altogether. The aggrivation from this debate stems from the confussion regarding what statistics are technically correct. Secondary data reports 45% of US internet households own at least one core smart home device. 
Phase 3 introduces Ecosystems such as Zigabee into the market. Big heads in business such as Amazon, Apple and Google begin to place their foot in the door with the introduction of Ecosystem solutions. This era revolutionalised developers approach to focus more on reliability and convenience between different appliances. 
Phase 4 is the current phase. AI driven homes have entered the market. The diection this follows is such: homes are aimed to work without the need to be 'asked'. Fully functional homes are the goal here, this includes traits such as presence detection, energy optimisation and predictive climate control from learned routines of clients. 
The customers who generally invest in smart home functionality are high profile clients. They value convenience, status and luxury. A main attraction point for them is the satrong energy management aspect, in hotter regions more cooling is required. A big concern from this audience is brand trust, privacy and consistent mainetnance which is currently lacking after installments. 
The biggest competitors in the game are companies such as Creston, Control4, Savant and KNX, particularly KNX who has had their place on the table for longer than others. 
Now in regards to statistics: Roots Analysis claims the market is currently worth $133.3 billion in 2026. ModelsAndModels used gathered data to predict a rise in value at 11.8% by 2032, where the value could rise to $450.20 billion. 
IDC expects China's market to exceed 300 million developments by 2026. 
Furthermore, a fun fact is that contrary to popular belief convenience plays as a much smaller buying driver than anticipated. Using sourced information, under an economical point of view, only 20% of energy costs are saved through smart home use, however, if paired with solar energy the return can rise far higher than the current roof placed on financial gain. 
Some global news: Google pulled out its software support for Nest learning Thermostats in 2025. 
